From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:46:49 -0500
Subject: feat: bring the layout of Arc's splits across

An Arc split came in side by side and half and half, whatever it was in Arc. Its
layout is in the file: splitView.layoutOrientation says side by side or stacked,
and splitView.itemWidthFactors gives each pane's share, as a list of pane ids each
followed by its share. A split nobody resized holds the first pane's alone, and a
pane with no share has an equal part of what is left. Of three or four panes the
first two make the split, and share what they hold between them. Numbers with no
ids are read by the panes' order, as some readers take them. Anything else stays
half and half.

Why: import I7 (BACKLOG S-103). The shape was checked against several public
readers of real files, so this no longer waits for a real file. One import of a
real file is still owed.
Removable when: the Arc importer leaves the series.
